# 2026-09-14: hash updated WITHOUT a version bump. The only surface file that
#   changed is src\index\DRagLint.Index.Freshness.pas, which extracts NOTHING:
#   it reads files.path / files.mtime_unix back out of an already-built index,
#   compares them against the filesystem, and returns a record plus one stderr
#   note. It emits no symbols, refs, uses or call edges, writes nothing to any
#   database, and parses no source. No existing index can hold a different
#   parse because of it, so a bump would buy a ~5 hour re-parse of every index
#   and change not one row.
#
#   What actually changed in it: the mtime reader. It used FileAge, which
#   applies the CURRENT utc offset; the indexer writes with
#   TFile.GetLastWriteTime, which applies the offset in force when the file was
#   written. The two disagreed by exactly one hour for every file dated in the
#   other daylight-saving period, so the staleness note claimed 3258 of 7001
#   library files had changed right after a clean full re-parse. Both readers
#   now share DRagLint.Core.FileTime.TryGetFileMTimeUnix.
#
#   NOTE FOR THE NEXT READER: the surface is the whole of src\index, and
#   src\index holds non-extracting utilities as well as the extractor. A hit
#   here is therefore a question, not automatically a bump -- but the broad
#   surface is deliberate, because it forces the question to be ASKED.
# 2026-09-16: hash updated WITHOUT a version bump, per the rule above.
#   src\index\DRagLint.Index.CallResolver.pas changed: member-access refs that
#   name a PROPERTY or FIELD now resolve (LookupMemberOnType / MemberAccessMode
#   / ResolveAccessor), writing refs.symbol_id, member_accesses and a
#   call_edges row for a method accessor. That is the RESOLVE pass -- derived
#   rows read off stored parses -- and it is governed by
#   DRAGLINT_RESOLVER_VERSION, which moved 1.2.0-alpha -> 1.3.0-alpha in the
#   same commit and re-derived every index (index --all --resolve-only). No
#   byte of source parses differently; no symbol or ref row changes; bumping
#   the EXTRACTOR version would buy a ~5-hour re-parse to alter not one stored
#   parse. Same shape as the Freshness.pas and ManifestWrite.pas entries above:
#   a src\index file that is not the extractor.
